<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rossano di Vaglio</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rossano di Vaglio is an archaeological site near Vaglio <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/basilicata">Basilicata</a>, north-east of Potenza in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>. It was the federal sanctuary of the Lucanians, dedicated to the goddess <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mefitis">Mefitis</a>, used from the 4th century BCE into the Roman period. The site has yielded many <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oscan-language">Oscan</a> inscriptions written in the Greek alphabet, as well as altars and votive offerings.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rossano-di-vaglio.jpg" alt="Rossano di Vaglio" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bla_z_er2001 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vaglio_Basilicata_(Potenza)_vicolo_del_nucleo_fortificato_01.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
